#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059406 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "13e5834d-4d70-5893-a4bf-9927000d522d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12704" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $3$ is an odd number.\n\n- **If** $2$ is an even number, **then** $3$ is an even number.\n\n- **If** $2$ is an odd number, **then** $3$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$3$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$2$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$3$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$2$ is an odd number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059407 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e1c01fd-dea0-5761-9499-d622a34fea3e" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table With Compound Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "0b97d670-694b-52e5-aa55-1224985f83a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12705" :question/problem "What are the missing values in the following truth table?\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add columns for $\\neg A$ and $A \\land B{:}$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land B \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $\\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B).$ This statement is true unless $\\neg A$ is true and $A \\land B$ is false.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\,$ | $\\, A \\land B \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow (A \\land B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059408 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"}] :question/id #uuid "8831a019-f252-5678-9855-6c0f1da89f77" :question/math-academy-id "e-12706" :question/problem "If $A$ is true, then $A \\Rightarrow B$ is $\\text{______________}.$\n\nWhich of the following could fill in the blank space above to make a true statement?\n\n- always true\n\n- always false\n\n- sometimes false" :question/worked-solution "The statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A = \\textrm T$ and $B = \\textrm T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A = \\textrm T$ and $B = \\textrm F,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{T}⇒\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is true, then $A \\Rightarrow B$ is $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm{sometimes false}}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A\\Rightarrow B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A \\Rightarrow B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c86885b-b599-5c06-9d18-46011698e3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571589} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5d7076-e5d0-5a8e-9b5e-817ab2472a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571610} {:answer/id #uuid "834baceb-70f0-5348-9456-86c55773d648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571762} {:answer/id #uuid "c683f13b-9a94-5a5d-b1c1-d01c067f15f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571892} {:answer/id #uuid "cde8f4b6-57b9-5b3c-9f78-3a1351406a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cde8f4b6-57b9-5b3c-9f78-3a1351406a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571908} :answer-field/id #uuid "b90a07ab-b9dc-568f-9e82-7d66cd0e1b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d3a8865-856a-528d-95c1-4dd040a3ff92" :question/math-academy-id "q-103483" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. **If** $3+5=7,$ **then** $2+4=7.$\n\nII. **If** $3+4=7,$ **then** $3+2=6.$\n\nIII. **If** $3+2=4,$ **then** $2+5=7.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent $3+5=7$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent $3+4=7$ is true, and the consequent $3+2=6$ is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $3+2=4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11b4773-38d5-5c0c-9e9c-3e0b4ecae818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab874b5-03d7-53c3-b6db-a652d9c156a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a11b4773-38d5-5c0c-9e9c-3e0b4ecae818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f8e36a-498b-5385-816f-6d262d6c4893" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96553132-07aa-5dd8-a9d9-80d5ba1e0f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453134} {:answer/id #uuid "f12b50d9-97e8-547c-ae5c-e9776f0678cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f12b50d9-97e8-547c-ae5c-e9776f0678cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae81137-1867-50f5-a1a9-e15ecfd57220" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "923f9c82-2491-5942-a700-0059eb11d931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453136} {:answer/id #uuid "bca078d7-e26d-5c8c-ac29-1d2b30f25905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca078d7-e26d-5c8c-ac29-1d2b30f25905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ffb718-a2da-578a-a502-45fd1b77e827" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103558" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **II.** **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **III.** **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b80483-fe65-55cb-9038-8211ba61f54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571802} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c2dd6-4a11-53bd-aa21-fab81d9eba5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571831} {:answer/id #uuid "fa3bcf1d-d459-521d-b1c3-9f9fbce7b8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571967} {:answer/id #uuid "fad78ea0-aa22-5b1d-9b2d-05112adc99e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa3bcf1d-d459-521d-b1c3-9f9fbce7b8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571967} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfd11c04-f5c0-5a2a-967d-efee14d871ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b0fcd8a-2ef6-570d-b9d5-23a0ce190bc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182389" :question/problem "If $A$ is false, then $A⇒B$ is\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nLet's break this down into cases:\n\n- When $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $A$ is false, then $A⇒B$ is $\\text{always true}.$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $F$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e9c7bbf-fb00-539d-87b4-f3bc2523bc2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376270} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a30bad-0f59-53be-afc3-27600bac37ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376271} {:answer/id #uuid "b2bf29ad-0150-5ba4-9be4-c00ede5f44d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376272} {:answer/id #uuid "ad50e2aa-6971-51a4-b3e5-cdf1c9a45d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad50e2aa-6971-51a4-b3e5-cdf1c9a45d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376273} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cbf9a7f-6130-5a5e-83ff-392722284603" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6582d0eb-c820-55a9-aa44-17c726abba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-182489" :question/problem "If $A$ is false and $B$ is true, then $A⇒B$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nSo, when $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44284cf6-1320-5447-9529-3d88349ac238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376276} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8662fb-2be5-5a3f-9186-1b82af5d5d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376277} {:answer/id #uuid "0c528769-c61a-58e9-b9b6-2655136673ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "always true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44284cf6-1320-5447-9529-3d88349ac238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sometimes true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376276} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e6fa9a-0002-56e1-a900-ced292e96381" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "606e4737-3